# Mobile view breakpoint

When the user says **mobile view**, **mobile**, or **mobile layout**, treat it as:

- **Mobile**: viewport width **&lt; 768px** (0–767px inclusive)
- **Not mobile** (tablet/desktop): **≥ 768px**

This is the default definition. **Do not change it** unless the user explicitly asks to use a different breakpoint.

## Implementation

Use these equivalents in code:

| Context | Mobile (&lt; 768px) | Desktop (≥ 768px) |
|---------|---------------------|-------------------|
| CSS | `@media (max-width: 767px)` | `@media (min-width: 768px)` |
| JS | `window.innerWidth < 768` | `window.innerWidth >= 768` |
| Tailwind | Default / unprefixed classes | `md:` prefix and up |

When implementing mobile-only or mobile-first changes, scope styles and behavior to **&lt; 768px** unless told otherwise.
